---
// Redrawn from Figure 10.1 of the dissertation. The original is a LaTeX figure
// that overflows its text block (the save-file box is clipped at the right
// margin) and is black-on-white, which would glare in dark mode. This version
// carries the same components and data flows using the site's design tokens, so
// it themes with the page and stays crisp at any size.
//
// Labels describe each component's role in the architecture rather than the
// module or vendor implementing it: implementations change, the decomposition
// is the durable part. The editor/save-file split is the intensional–extensional
// one — shared rules and schemas on one side, per-session asserted facts on the
// other — which is why the authoring layer is read-only once simulation starts.
---

<figure class="arch">
  <svg
    class="arch__svg"
    viewBox="0 0 900 500"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  >
    <title id="arch-title">Insimul runtime architecture</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      The authoring layer supplies shared world templates — schemas, rules, actions, and grammars —
      to the unified simulation engine, and is read-only once simulation begins. The engine
      discharges goals through a Prolog runtime performing SLD resolution over Horn clauses with
      negation as failure, and asserts the resulting facts to playthrough state, which is the sole
      write target. Narratives and events flow out to clients and intents flow back in. Statistical
      generation and speech input/output attach as pluggable side components, conditioned on the
      symbolic state.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="arw" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arch__head" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- client surface -->
    <rect x="340" y="8" width="220" height="82" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="450" y="34" text-anchor="middle">Client Surface</text>
    <text class="arch__s" x="450" y="55" text-anchor="middle">request–response · streaming</text>
    <text class="arch__mono" x="450" y="72" text-anchor="middle">REST · WS · SSE · gRPC</text>

    <!-- authoring layer -->
    <rect x="10" y="150" width="210" height="104" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="115" y="176" text-anchor="middle">Authoring Layer</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="115" y="197">shared world templates</tspan>
      <tspan x="115" y="213">schemas · rules · actions</tspan>
      <tspan x="115" y="229">read-only at simulation time</tspan>
    </text>

    <!-- engine -->
    <rect x="325" y="173" width="250" height="58" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--key" />
    <text class="arch__t arch__t--key" x="450" y="196" text-anchor="middle">Unified Simulation Engine</text>
    <text class="arch__s arch__s--key" x="450" y="216" text-anchor="middle">query · volition · effect application</text>

    <!-- playthrough state -->
    <rect x="680" y="150" width="210" height="104" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="785" y="180" text-anchor="middle">Playthrough State</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="785" y="203">per-session asserted facts</tspan>
      <tspan x="785" y="219">sole write target</tspan>
    </text>

    <!-- prolog runtime -->
    <rect x="325" y="286" width="250" height="96" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="450" y="312" text-anchor="middle">Prolog Runtime</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="450" y="333">SLD resolution over Horn clauses</tspan>
      <tspan x="450" y="349">negation as failure</tspan>
    </text>
    <text class="arch__mono" x="450" y="368" text-anchor="middle">Trealla</text>

    <!-- side components -->
    <rect x="60" y="410" width="210" height="72" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--soft" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="165" y="436" text-anchor="middle">Statistical Generation</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="165" y="457">provider-agnostic</tspan>
      <tspan x="165" y="473">conditioned on symbolic state</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="630" y="410" width="210" height="72" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--soft" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="735" y="436" text-anchor="middle">Speech I/O</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="735" y="457">recognition · synthesis</tspan>
      <tspan x="735" y="473">utterance ⇄ symbolic intent</tspan>
    </text>

    <!-- flows -->
    <path d="M220,202 H318" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="269" y="178">rules,</tspan>
      <tspan x="269" y="191">seed facts</tspan>
    </text>

    <path d="M575,202 H673" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="624" y="178">asserted</tspan>
      <tspan x="624" y="191">mutations</tspan>
    </text>

    <path d="M408,173 V97" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" x="400" y="140" text-anchor="end">narratives, events</text>

    <path d="M500,97 V166" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" x="510" y="140" text-anchor="start">intents</text>

    <path d="M450,231 V279" class="arch__line" marker-start="url(#arw)" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" x="462" y="259" text-anchor="start">goals ⇄ bindings</text>

    <path d="M325,352 C255,352 235,382 205,404" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <path d="M575,352 C645,352 665,382 695,404" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="arch__cap">
    <span class="arch__credit">Runtime Architecture</span>
    The authoring layer holds shared world templates and is read-only once play begins; playthrough
    state holds per-session asserted facts and is the only thing the engine writes to. Statistical
    generation and speech attach as pluggable components, conditioned on the symbolic state rather
    than driving it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .arch {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .arch__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .arch__box {
    fill: var(--bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--border-strong);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .arch__box--key {
    fill: var(--accent-soft);
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }

  .arch__box--soft {
    fill: none;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .arch__t {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--text);
  }

  .arch__t--key {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }

  .arch__s {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .arch__s--key {
    fill: var(--text);
  }

  .arch__mono,
  .arch__lbl {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .arch__mono {
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .arch__lbl {
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .arch__line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-faint);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
  }

  .arch__head {
    fill: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .arch__cap {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .arch__credit {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
